# BotShieldFlagTrigger — a starting slate, not a compiled-in default.
#
# Nothing here is enforced automatically. The module ships no default
# rules: an unset score threshold never fires, so a fresh deployment
# scores nothing and challenges nothing until you declare both a flag
# (or heuristic) trigger and a threshold. That is deliberate — a
# default every deployment has to disable was not a default, and every
# lockout this module has caused traced back to an implicit weight
# nobody had written down. This file is what the module used to seed
# automatically, kept as a documented starting point for anyone who
# wants that shape rather than building it from a blank slate. It is
# NOT a required include, and it does nothing until you paste some or
# all of it into your own config. tests/setup/botshield-dev.conf carries the
# same slate wired into a live vhost, if you want to see it running
# rather than read about it.
#
# To extend: add `BotShieldFlagTrigger` lines to your vhost or server
# config. Score actions accumulate (SUM); tier_floor actions take MAX
# (strictest tier wins). A later declaration for the same flag adds to
# an earlier one from this same file unless you use the `reset`
# keyword to clear it first.
#
# Syntax:
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag_name> [reset] [action=<verb> args...]
#
# Action verbs:
#   action=score add=N             (signed; SUM across matching triggers)
#   action=tier_floor min=<tier>   (pass|noninteractive|interactive|captcha; MAX)
#
# Reset keyword (clears every prior declaration — from this file or
# your own config — for the same flag, processed at config-load time):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> reset                              # bare
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> reset action=<verb> ...            # +inline
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> reset                              # multi-
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> action=...                         # line
#
# Observe-mode (logs `wouldflagtrigger:<flag>:observe` instead of
# applying the side effect — useful for safe rollout of a new rule):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger <flag> action=score add=N mode=observe

# --- Detection signals — definitive ---------------------------------
# Honeypot hits and fake-bot signatures (UA claims a search-engine
# crawler from a non-search-engine network, etc.) are essentially
# never legitimate traffic. Push the score and force captcha so the
# response stops short of any user content.
BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit          action=score      add=60
BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit          action=tier_floor min=captcha
BotShieldFlagTrigger fake_bot              action=score      add=80
BotShieldFlagTrigger fake_bot              action=tier_floor min=captcha

# --- Detection signals — probable -----------------------------------
# Scanner probes (vulnerability-scan path patterns) are usually bots
# but occasionally legitimate research traffic. Push score and require
# an interactive-tier solve — strong friction without the captcha
# accessibility cost.
BotShieldFlagTrigger scanner_probe         action=score      add=50
BotShieldFlagTrigger scanner_probe         action=tier_floor min=interactive

# --- Detection signals — accumulating -------------------------------
# Repeat PoW failures from one cookie. Could be a broken client
# (JS disabled, time-skewed, CSP-stripped) or a scripted attacker
# trying to brute the challenge. Bump to noninteractive — the next
# solve proves human behavior cheaply, and the score addition primes
# the request near the tier-bump threshold.
BotShieldFlagTrigger pow_fail_streak       action=score      add=30
BotShieldFlagTrigger pow_fail_streak       action=tier_floor min=noninteractive

# --- Trust signals (credits) ----------------------------------------
# Application-issued reputation. The app sees session-bound state the
# module can't (logged-in user, prior good behavior, etc.) and feeds
# back via the X-BotShield-Feedback header surface. Credits subtract
# score; they never RAISE tier — a credit shouldn't force a request UP.
# Multiple credits compose additively (SUM).
BotShieldFlagTrigger app_verified_human    action=score      add=-80
BotShieldFlagTrigger app_verified_session  action=score      add=-40
BotShieldFlagTrigger app_trust_signal      action=score      add=-20

# --- Common overrides -----------------------------------------------
#
# Soften captcha to interactive on honeypot_hit (e.g., behind a CDN
# where captcha is troublesome):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit reset action=score add=60
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger honeypot_hit       action=tier_floor min=interactive
#
# Disable pow_fail_streak escalation entirely (e.g., when running
# behind a JS-restricting client that legitimately fails the PoW):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger pow_fail_streak reset
#
# Stronger app credit, on top of the -80 line above (push score down
# 120 total instead of 80):
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger app_verified_human action=score add=-40
#   # combined effect: -80 (this file) + -40 (your line) = -120
#
# Try a new rule in observe-mode for one release before enforcing:
#   BotShieldFlagTrigger scanner_probe action=tier_floor min=captcha mode=observe
#   # logs `wouldflagtrigger:scanner_probe:observe` on every fire;
#   # remove `mode=observe` once the rate looks right.
